Z||000008||Formula88||08-25-2001||11:48 AM||||That would be, in human terms:<BR>12<BR>13<BR>12<P><B>Code 12</B> - No reference pulses to ECM.  This is also the "A-OK" code you should always get when checking codes.  There's no reference pulse to the ECM, because the engine's not running.<P><B>Code 13</B> - Oxygen Sensor Circuit:<BR>Check for a sticking or misadjusted throttle posistion sensor.  Check the wiring and connectors from the oxygen sensor.  Replace the oxygen sensor.<P><FONT SIZE="1">--Helms, Ch. 6, pg. 160--</FONT>||||reg||3
Z||000009||Oreif||08-25-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroburton:<BR><B>just did it this is what i got before it started to repeat itself<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__***<BR>*__***<BR>*__***<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>what does this mean ?<BR>ps that was easy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>*_** = 12 (Normal)<P>*_*** = 13 Oxygen sensor. The oxygen sensor is either bad or the TPS (throttle position sensor) is bad.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroburton||08-25-2001||12:15 PM||||how long can i drive without replacing this ?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mach10||08-25-2001||01:27 PM||||Forever, but your gas mileage will go to **** . If it's the TPS that's making the ECM think the O-2's off, then the car may start to act weird (bucking off the line, jerky acceleration, stumbling) and have crap gas mileage. If it IS the O-2 sensor (and it almost always is, they need replacing every 20k) then the car will start running really rich, and act a little funny. That's about it.<BR>Be prepared to shell out a whopping $25.00 for a new O2 Sensor! Just be careful threading it in. You do NOT want to strip it!||||reg||7
