Z||000016||fieroburton||08-25-2001||02:56 PM||||my new question is what is the best way to take out and replace a o2 cencor ?<BR>or is the hayns or chiltens manuel the way to go ?<BR>if it is as easy as taking a alternator out then im going to pay some one to do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||Mach10||08-25-2001||03:07 PM||||It's one bolt, and a wire-harness. Just be careful not to break the harness. Don't worry about destroying the old sensor. Just rip the wire off it, and slap a socket on it. For putting it on, just use the appropriate box-end and tighten it, but not too hard.<P>EDIT:<BR>Oh, wait. Those insructions are for the v6. What do you have? I can't see it being much more difficult. If in doubt, just follow either manual.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||6
